&lt;li&gt;This section of the Railway is a part of &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.walkwheelcycletrust.org.uk/find-a-route-on-the-national-cycle-network/route-27/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;National Cycle Network, Route 27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="south-devon-plymouth--tavistock-railway"&gt;South Devon (Plymouth) -Tavistock Railway
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This section of the railway was opened in 1859 and originally of &lt;a class="link" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broad-gauge_railway" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;broad gauge&lt;/a&gt; which could be anything &lt;em&gt;wider&lt;/em&gt; than the &lt;code&gt;standard gauge&lt;/code&gt; of 4ft 8.5&amp;quot; (1,435mm). Shortly after opening, it was adapted in 1876 to also carry &lt;code&gt;standard gauge&lt;/code&gt; (also known as &lt;code&gt;narrow guage&lt;/code&gt;) by adding a third rail. The British Railways were generally standardising their track gauges though, and by 1892, this section had converted fully to &lt;code&gt;standard gauge&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="link" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Devon_and_Tavistock_Railway" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Wikipedia - South Devon (Plymouth) -Tavistock Railway&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/10.jpg"
width="750"
height="563"
srcset="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/10_hu_9f2b11d8f21f0df1.jpg 480w, https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/10_hu_9cb3c76e6aec019c.jpg 1024w"
loading="lazy"
alt="Looking back at the bridge, along the cycle route, at the site of Shaugh Platform"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="133"
data-flex-basis="319px"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Shaugh Bridge Platform opened in 1907 and was closed at the end of 1962.&lt;/p&gt;
