&lt;h2 id="leighbeer-tunnel"&gt;Leighbeer Tunnel
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/12.jpg"
width="750"
height="563"
srcset="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/12_hu_c68041cfc9020065.jpg 480w, https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/12_hu_26b2aee3ba5deeea.jpg 1024w"
loading="lazy"
alt="Entering Leighbeer Tunnel"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="133"
data-flex-basis="319px"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leighbeer Tunnel, also known as &amp;ldquo;The Smokies&amp;rdquo; is 282m in length. The metal aquaduct close to the portal carries water for the Wheal Lopes leat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/13.jpg"
width="750"
height="563"
srcset="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/13_hu_42cbd9872ff104d0.jpg 480w, https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/13_hu_9757bf45fd26b1d8.jpg 1024w"
loading="lazy"
alt="Inside Leighbeer Tunnel"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="133"
data-flex-basis="319px"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The light at the end of the tunnel, showing the lights along the way and the refuges in the sidewalls for men to shelter when trains used to run the through the tunnel - this being the old &lt;a class="link" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Devon_and_Tavistock_Railway" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;South Devon (Plymouth) -Tavistock Railway&lt;/a&gt;, broad gauge, opened in 1859.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/14.jpg"
width="750"
height="563"
srcset="https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/14_hu_33f15fe1d5004c56.jpg 480w, https://dartmoorwalking.org/p/clearbrook-and-leighbeer/14_hu_fc2b0198a835ad35.jpg 1024w"
loading="lazy"
alt="Side Adit"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="133"
data-flex-basis="319px"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Part way along the tunnel, there is an adit. This is part of Bickleigh Vale Phoenix Mine, also known as Leighbeer Tunnel Mine, a copper mine that may also have produced lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whilst digging the tunnel, workmen discovered some copper ore and dug this short adit to explore that potential. A small company was formed and the mine opened in the same year as the tunnel, but only operated for around three years as the lode was found to be thin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pictures of the adit are available&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class="link" href="https://www.28dayslater.co.uk/threads/bickleigh-vale-mine-leighbeer-tunnel.52027/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;28dayslater&lt;/a&gt; and a &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.28dayslater.co.uk/threads/bickleigh-vale-phoenix-mine-july-09.41712/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;second report&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
